# ============================================================================
# GWIscan family table — FAMILY mode (one flat list of families)
# ============================================================================
# Copy this file to  config/family.tsv  and edit it for your study families,
# and set  MODE: family  in config.yaml.
#
# One row per family. TAB-separated. Whole-line '#' comments and blank lines are
# ignored (put each comment on its own line beginning with '#').
#
# COLUMNS
#   Family      Study family name. Used verbatim in outputs and in systematic
#               domain ids (e.g. GNA -> AthGNA001.1). Required and unique.
#
#   PfamModel   How the family is identified and confirmed — one of three forms,
#               told apart automatically:
#                 PFxxxxx   a Pfam accession. The HMM is downloaded from InterPro
#                           and pressed for hmmscan; DIAMOND also runs; the merged
#                           candidates are then CONFIRMED by InterProScan reporting
#                           that same Pfam. Use only when the Pfam is specific to
#                           the family.
#                 name.hmm  a custom, family-specific HMM you built and placed in
#                           db/hmm/. Identified by hmmscan (this HMM) + DIAMOND,
#                           then MERGED — NO InterProScan. Its own hmmscan hit
#                           gives the domain coordinates. Its NAME line inside the
#                           .hmm must equal the Family. Use this when the family's
#                           Pfam is a shared/ancestral domain not specific to the
#                           family (identify with a curated profile instead).
#                 -         no HMM. Identified by DIAMOND alone; merged as final;
#                           no InterProScan.
#
#   BlastModel  Reference protein FASTA (in db/blast/) used as the DIAMOND round-1
#               query. DIAMOND runs for every family, so this is required for all.
#
# Rule: InterProScan runs ONLY for families whose PfamModel is a Pfam accession.
# Custom-HMM and DIAMOND-only families never touch InterProScan.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Family	PfamModel	BlastModel
# specific Pfam -> hmmscan + DIAMOND, InterProScan-confirmed:
GNA	PF01453	AAA33346.1.fasta
Legume	PF00139	AAA33983.1.fasta
# custom curated HMM (in db/hmm/CRA.hmm) -> hmmscan + DIAMOND, merged, no InterProScan:
CRA	CRA.hmm	ABL98074.1.fasta
# no HMM -> DIAMOND only, merged, no InterProScan:
EUL	-	ABW73993.1.fasta
